      "text": "Start by finding the inverse of the function.\n\nSequence of steps: Find the inverse \n\nWe know that if two functions are inverses of each other, then the composition of $f$ and $g$ is the identity function. Because of this, if we perform two inverse functions and they result in no change to the variable (followed by a set of parentheses to ensure proper order of operations), the result is the variable itself. That is, \n\n$g^{-1}(a) = a$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$\\begin{array}{ccccccccccc}\\textbf{Set}: &0 & = & \f3a-\f4 &\\quad & \\text{Use the given formula $g(x)=3x-4$} \\\\ \\textbf{Add 4}$ to both sides: &-\f4  & &\f3a & &   \\quad &\\text{After adding 4 to both sides, we have the variable isolated and 4 added to the left-hand side; the variable is isolated by addition, meaning that the inverse function must be subtraction} \\\\ \\textbf{Divide by 3}:\f\f\f    &                                                       &\f        &\f\f\f\f\f        &\f\fall     &\f                                                            &\f    \\quad &\\text{After dividing both sides by 3, we are left with only $a$ multiplied by 3$}$ \\\\ \\textbf{Set $a$ out}:\f\f\f\f\f\f\f\f\f\f\f\f\f\f\f\f\f&                                                                        &\f\f\f\f\f\f\f\f                                                        &\f\f\f\f\f\f\f\f\f\f\f\f\f\f\f\f\f\f\f\f\f\f\f\f\f\f\f$\\therefore$ & \n\n$\\begin{gathered}\\boxed{a=1}\\end{gathered}$\n\nSolution Receive a verification link. Type the verification code.\n\\boxed{1}",
